From: Zenith
Subject: [PATCH] ES: scaledLogoSpacing follows the animated camera (no jump of the old/new selected item when moving)

The shift of the neighbours of the selected item was decided with the cursor (instant) while the positions use mCamOffset (animated), so on
each key press the old selected item jumped logoDiffX to the left/right and the new one jumped back. Continuous shift: logoDiffX * clamp(i - camOffset, -1, 1).
---
--- a/es-core/src/components/CarouselComponent.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/components/CarouselComponent.cpp
@@ -489,12 +489,11 @@
 		{
 			auto logoDiffX = ((logoSpacing[0] * mLogoScale) - logoSpacing[0]) / 2.0f * mScaledSpacing;
 
-			if (index == mCursor)
-				logoTrans.translate(Vector3f(i * logoSpacing[0] + xOff, i * logoSpacing[1] + yOff, 0));
-			else if (i < mCursor || (mCursor == 0 && index > mMaxLogoCount))
-				logoTrans.translate(Vector3f(i * logoSpacing[0] + xOff - logoDiffX, i * logoSpacing[1] + yOff, 0));
-			else
-				logoTrans.translate(Vector3f(i * logoSpacing[0] + xOff + logoDiffX, i * logoSpacing[1] + yOff, 0));
+			// The neighbours move away from the selected item by logoDiffX. It used to depend on the cursor, which changes at once when a key is
+			// pressed, while the item positions follow the animated camera: the old and the new selected item jumped by logoDiffX. Now the shift is
+			// a continuous function of the distance to the camera (0 on it, +-logoDiffX from one position away).
+			const float rel = Math::clamp(i - mCamOffset, -1.0f, 1.0f);
+			logoTrans.translate(Vector3f(i * logoSpacing[0] + xOff + logoDiffX * rel, i * logoSpacing[1] + yOff, 0));
 		}
 		else
 			logoTrans.translate(Vector3f(i * logoSpacing[0] + xOff, i * logoSpacing[1] + yOff, 0));
